{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaGapVandermonde","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaGapVandermonde","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaBetaProdMonoid"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_one_sub_pow_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_one_sub_pow_pair","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaGapVandermonde.lean#L111-L126","doc":"**The q-analogue, in Vandermonde-ready form.**\n\n`∏_c (1 − Q^{h_λ(c)}) · ∏_{i<j} (1 − Q^{β_i − β_j}) = ∏_i ∏_{k=1}^{β_i} (1 − Q^k)`.\n\nThis is the hook-length input that\n`QOU.Mathlib.LagrangeCoeffSum.sum_eq_bracket_mul_of_qratio_scaling` needs, cleared of division.\nWith `x_i = Q^{β_i}` the middle factor is `∏_{i<j}(x_i − x_j)` up to the monomial `∏_{i<j} x_j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_mul_pair_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_mul_pair_prod","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaGapVandermonde.lean#L99-L109","doc":"**The divisor-free FRT hook product with a Vandermonde denominator, any commutative monoid.**\n\n`∏_c f(h_λ(c)) · ∏_{i<j} f(β_i − β_j) = ∏_i descFactF f β_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prod_betaGapProdF_eq_pair_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prod_betaGapProdF_eq_pair_prod","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaGapVandermonde.lean#L85-L97","doc":"**The β-gap product in Vandermonde pair form.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGap_eq_betaNum_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGap_eq_betaNum_sub","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaGapVandermonde.lean#L72-L83","doc":"**The `k`-th β-gap factor of row `i` is `β_i − β_{i+1+k}`.**\n\n`β_i − β_j = (l[i] − l[j]) + (j − i)` for `j > i`, and the recursion's `a + (k+1) − t[k]` is exactly\nthat with `j = i+1+k`.  Needs `l[j] ≤ l[i]`, i.e. that `l` is weakly decreasing — without it the two\ntruncated subtractions part company. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF_drop_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF_drop_eq","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaGapVandermonde.lean#L63-L70","doc":"Row `i`'s β-gap product, indexed by the offset `k` into the rows below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.getD_drop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.getD_drop","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaGapVandermonde.lean#L60-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF_eq_prod_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaGapProdF_eq_prod_range","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaGapVandermonde.lean#L45-L58","doc":"The β-gap recursion, unrolled into a `Finset.range` product: the `k`-th factor is\n`f(a + (k+1) − t[k])`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaNum","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBetaGapVandermonde.lean#L41-L43","doc":"The β-number of row `i`: `β_i = l[i] + (|l| − 1 − i)`.  Strictly decreasing in `i` for a\nweakly-decreasing `l`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}